The current bug report mentions an inconsistency in how line terminators are handled in the `ExtendedBufferReader`. It highlights that the `readLine()` method treats carriage return (CR), line feed (LF), and carriage return followed by line feed (CRLF) equally, but the class should also allow for CR alone as a line terminator for flexibility.

