```java
public CSVParser(String input, CSVFormat format) throws IOException{
    this(new StringReader(input), format);
}
```

The issue could lie in how the `CSVParser` is handling the custom line separator `"\r"`. The test uses `"\r"` as the line separator, which might not be handled properly in the `CSVParser` implementation, potentially leading to the failure in identifying the line number correctly.

